# PhotoCraft, the image editor, and its command line, compiled by Cargo from the pinned sources,
# offline. The app draws on the page through Dolly's platforms in winit (display@0, input@0) and
# wgpu (gpu@0). File › Open takes a file the user picks in the browser (upload@0), its other
# dialogs are the zenity command, and each file a save writes is offered to the browser too
# (download@0). The command line converts and inspects images and PSD files, runs commands and
# batches, renders on gpu@0 where the browser grants WebGPU, and serves its commands to agents
# over MCP. zenity, built by a run of its own so that egui keeps PhotoCraft's features, is the
# dialogs, on the same platforms. Where DISPLAY names an X server (x11-desktop) the app and zenity
# are windows of it (x11-window, over Xlib), their frames read back from gpu@0; copy and paste
# are the page's clipboard (clipboard@0) on the page and there.
